From 8e58a33d8295542be806e142f6d040d200949356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HempFiend <17104973+jaidenscool1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:30:24 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] nx2: passthrough backend: virtual textures transcoded per
 cell into sparse BC3 copies

ASTC textures too large to transcode whole (MKW's 8192^2 x 84 virtual-texture arrays, 1.75 GiB each,
and its 8192^2 single-layer images) were left raw and sampled black on the host GPU. Such a header now
points at a BC3 copy in a sparse host range above the guest's (unbacked pages read 0). Workers
(EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_VT_THREADS, 2) transcode the texture in cells of 64x64 ASTC blocks of one level of
one layer whose guest bytes are non-zero and changed, swizzle them into a CPU reservation laid out as the
header's block-linear image (Eglantine's subrect swizzles with its upload stride alignment: MKW's
arrays use tile width spacing 4), and import and map only the 64 KiB pages a cell touched. Cells are
looked at when the texture is first sampled, when the guest maps memory over it, and after copy-engine
launches into it. Levels spread over several guest mappings are gathered page by page. A layout
self-test against whole-level swizzles runs at the first such texture; textures it cannot handle stay
raw. EDEN_NX2_PASSTHROUGH_VTSCAN=1 logs the written GOBs of each (measuring).

MKW boot to race: 5 textures, 6501 cells, 1378 MiB of BC3 mapped, ~46 s of worker time; the track
surface, canyon and buildings are textured on the host GPU; no Xid.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/video_core/nx2_passthrough.cpp | 540 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 536 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

